subject: feat(rate-limiter): multi-bucket per-(ip,category) limits with shared route classifier

Replace the single general/chat buckets with a proper route classifier so
each traffic class gets an independent per-IP budget. Auth brute-force can
no longer starve dashboard traffic, and LLM completions can't eat the API
allowance.

- src/lib/middleware/routeClassifier.js (ESM, Next middleware layer) +
  an inline CJS twin in custom-server.rate-limiter.js (loads before ESM
  is available). Behaviour pinned to identical fixtures by the test suites.
- Buckets: static/rsc bypass entirely (framework traffic, Finding #16);
  auth 10/min — narrowed to POST login/setup/reset-password only, since
  /api/auth/status is polled by Header.js every page load and stays in
  api; chat 20/min (POST completions only, GET uses api); api 120/min
  (other /api/* + /v1/*); general 120/min fallback.
- rateLimiter.js rewritten to per-(ip, category) buckets; checkRateLimit
  classifies on pathname+search so the classifier sees ?_rsc= prefetches.
- custom-server.rate-limiter.js (TCP layer) rewritten to ip|category
  counters; cli/app copy synced (gitignored build artifact, regenerated
  by cli:pack).

Tests: TCP original 9/9 + multi-bucket 8/8 + route-classifier 35/35 +
middleware 24/24 = 76/76 passing. ESLint clean on all touched files.

